PRODUCT REQUIREMENTS DOCUMENT
AI-Powered Mock Test Platform for Government Job Aspirants
Version 1.0  |  September 2026
1. Overview
This document defines the Product Requirements for Version 1 (V1) of an AI-powered Mock Test Platform targeted at students preparing for government jobs and placement exams. The platform enables topic-wise timed practice tests with performance analytics and AI-generated feedback.
2. Problem Statement
Students preparing for government exams and placements need focused, topic-wise practice with timed conditions. Existing platforms often provide only full-length mocks or static question banks without personalized feedback on weak areas and time management. There is a need for a simple platform where students can practice specific topics at chosen difficulty levels, track time spent per question, and receive actionable AI feedback.
3. Goals (V1)
	•	Allow students to take topic-wise timed practice tests
	•	Dynamically generate mocks based on student-selected Topic, Level, Number of Questions, and Time
	•	Track time spent on each question
	•	Provide score, solutions for wrong answers, and AI feedback on strongest & weakest areas
	•	Enable Admin to manage questions (CRUD) with Topic and Difficulty
	•	Maintain history of student attempts and basic progress tracking
4. Non-Goals (Out of Scope for V1)
	•	AI-generated questions
	•	Full-length government exam simulation (100–200 question papers)
	•	Advanced analytics dashboards and complex charts
	•	Leaderboards, streaks, gamification, or social features
	•	Mobile native apps
	•	Payment / subscription system
	•	Multi-language support
5. User Roles
5.1 Admin
	•	Sign up / Login
	•	Create, Read, Update, Delete questions (with Topic + Difficulty Level)
	•	Create and manage Topics
	•	View list of questions/topics they have created
5.2 Student
	•	Sign up / Login
	•	Select Topic + Level + Number of Questions + Time and start a test
	•	Take the test, submit answers, view results
	•	View AI feedback on performance
	•	View personal dashboard with past attempts and progress
6. Detailed Features (V1)
6.1 Authentication & Roles
	•	User Signup and Login
	•	Role-based access control (Admin / Student)
	•	Students can only submit tests and view their own dashboard
6.2 Question Management (Admin)
	•	Admin creates Topics
	•	Admin performs full CRUD on Questions
	•	Each question has: Topic, Difficulty Level (Easy / Medium / Difficult), question text, options, correct answer, and optional explanation
	•	Admin can view all questions they have created
6.3 Starting a Test (Student)
	•	Student selects: Topic + Difficulty Level + Number of Questions (1–20) + Time limit
	•	System dynamically creates a mock by randomly selecting available questions matching the criteria
	•	If fewer questions exist than requested, system informs the student of available count
	•	Even if only 1–2 questions exist, student can still attempt the mock
6.4 Test Taking Experience
	•	Questions are shown one by one
	•	Overall timer for the entire test
	•	Auto-submit when time ends
	•	Skip option available — student can leave a question and return later via the Question Palette
	•	Question Palette is available — student can jump to any question at any time (answered, skipped, or marked for review)
	•	Number of questions in a mock is not fixed; it varies based on student selection and available questions
	•	Final scoring rule: If the student answers a previously skipped question correctly before submission, it is counted as correct. Only questions left unanswered at the time of submission are counted as wrong
6.5 Result Page
	•	Score displayed as Correct / Total
	•	Solutions shown only for wrong answers
	•	Time spent on each question is displayed
	•	AI feedback on strongest and weakest areas is generated immediately after submission
6.6 AI Feedback
After every test submission, the following data is sent to the AI:
	•	Correct topics
	•	Wrong topics
	•	Time spent per question
	•	Accuracy
AI returns personalized suggestions on strongest areas, weakest areas, and how to improve.
6.7 Student Dashboard
	•	List of all mocks attempted
	•	Marks of previous attempts with Date & Time
	•	Score and Accuracy per topic
	•	Time spent on each question (historical)
	•	Simple daily/weekly progress view (score trend – increasing or decreasing)
6.8 Admin Dashboard
	•	Admin can view all questions/topics they have created (with topic name and difficulty)
7. Rules & Edge Cases
	•	Minimum questions per mock: 1
	•	Maximum questions per mock: 20
	•	If requested number of questions is higher than available, inform student of actual available count
	•	Student can re-attempt the same Topic + Level combination
	•	Re-attempts do not overwrite previous scores; full history is preserved
	•	Questions left unanswered at final submission (including previously skipped ones that were never answered) are counted as incorrect. Answering a skipped question correctly later counts as correct
8. Key User Flows
8.1 Student Flow
	•	Signup / Login
	•	Select Topic + Level + No. of Questions + Time
	•	System creates mock and starts timer
	•	Answer questions one by one with Question Palette (can skip and return later to answer)
	•	Submit (or auto-submit on timeout)
	•	View Score + Wrong answers with solutions + Time per question
	•	Receive AI feedback on strong & weak areas
	•	View Dashboard for history and progress
8.2 Admin Flow
	•	Login
	•	Create / Edit / Delete Topics
	•	Create / Edit / Delete Questions (Topic + Level + content)
	•	View list of created questions
9. Success Metrics (V1)
	•	Student can complete a full cycle: Login → Select criteria → Take test → View result + AI feedback
	•	Admin can add at least 50+ questions across multiple topics
	•	Time tracking accuracy is reliable
	•	AI feedback is generated within a few seconds after submission
10. Proposed Tech Stack
Backend: FastAPI (Python)
Database: PostgreSQL
ORM: SQLAlchemy or SQLModel
Authentication: JWT
AI Feedback: OpenAI / Gemini API
Frontend: To be decided (React / Next.js recommended for later polish)
11. Future Scope (V2+)
	•	AI-generated questions based on Topic + Level
	•	Full government exam style mocks (fixed large question sets)
	•	Advanced progress charts and topic-wise mastery tracking
	•	Question difficulty auto-classification from student performance data
	•	Bookmark weak questions and personalized practice recommendations
	•	Mobile application
